Note, a complete Pong game written in E plus plus itself.
Note, move your paddle with the arrow keys up and down.
Note, the ball speeds up a little every time you hit it.

Open window with title Pong.
Add canvas board with width 600 and height 400.

Let ball x be 300.
Let ball y be 200.
Let ball speed x be 5.
Let ball speed y be 3.
Let player y be 160.
Let robot y be 160.
Let score be 0.
Let lives be 3.

Every 20 milliseconds, do the following.

Note, move the player paddle.
If key arrow up is pressed, do the following.
Subtract 8 from player y.
End if.
If key arrow down is pressed, do the following.
Add 8 to player y.
End if.
If the value of player y is less than 0, do the following.
Set player y to 0.
End if.
If the value of player y is greater than 320, do the following.
Set player y to 320.
End if.

Note, the robot paddle follows the ball slowly.
If the value of robot y plus 40 is less than ball y, do the following.
Add 4 to robot y.
End if.
If the value of robot y plus 40 is greater than ball y, do the following.
Subtract 4 from robot y.
End if.

Note, move the ball.
Add the value of ball speed x to ball x.
Add the value of ball speed y to ball y.
If the value of ball y is less than 5, do the following.
Set ball speed y to 0 minus ball speed y.
End if.
If the value of ball y is greater than 395, do the following.
Set ball speed y to 0 minus ball speed y.
End if.

Note, bounce off the player paddle on the left.
If the value of ball x is less than 30, do the following.
If the value of ball y is greater than player y, do the following.
If the value of ball y is less than player y plus 80, do the following.
Set ball speed x to 0 minus ball speed x.
Add 1 to score.
End if.
End if.
End if.

Note, bounce off the robot paddle on the right.
If the value of ball x is greater than 570, do the following.
Set ball speed x to 0 minus ball speed x.
End if.

Note, a miss on the left costs one life.
If the value of ball x is less than 0, do the following.
Subtract 1 from lives.
Set ball x to 300.
Set ball y to 200.
Say Lives left.
Say the value of lives.
End if.

Note, redraw everything.
Clear canvas.
Draw rectangle at 10 by the value of player y with width 12 and height 80 and color green.
Draw rectangle at 578 by the value of robot y with width 12 and height 80 and color red.
Draw circle at the value of ball x by the value of ball y with radius 8 and color yellow.
Draw text Score at 60 by 20 with color white.
Draw text the value of score at 120 by 20 with color white.

If the value of lives is less than 1, do the following.
Clear canvas.
Draw text Game over at 300 by 200 with color red.
Say Game over.
Say the value of score.
Stop ticking.
End if.

End every.
